id: pm-o87av6
title: "Outcome milestone: proven scale — sub-second bounded-token context at a million items with thousands of concurrent agents"
description: ""
type: Milestone
status: open
priority: 2
tags[7]: concurrency,context-management,"horizon:long",milestone,outcome,performance,scale
created_at: "2026-07-24T23:43:41.928Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T23:44:34.766Z"
deadline: "2027-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 9600
acceptance_criteria: "list/context/next/get-by-filter are served from a derived index with cost proportional to the result, not the workspace; Published benchmark evidence at 1M items shows sub-second bounded-token context assembly on commodity hardware; Claim and lock throughput is measured under thousands of concurrent agents with documented contention behaviour; The small end is proven too: a three-item scratch workspace pays proportional, near-zero ceremony and token cost; History and repository growth stay bounded by an automated compaction, gc, and archival policy"
goal: proven-scale
objective: "Context assembly cost is bounded by the answer size, not the workspace size, at every scale from three items to a million"
value: "Scale is the claim that distinguishes pm from a flat-file backlog: an agent must not pay for workspace size it never reads."
impact: "Determines whether pm can host decade-spanning, multi-team, thousands-of-agents workspaces or stays a single-repo tool."
outcome: "Published, reproducible benchmark evidence for latency, memory, token cost, and claim throughput at the million-item and thousand-agent points."
why_now: The read path still scans item files; every capability added before the index lands inherits the scan and has to be re-tuned afterwards.
parent: pm-doxj
risk: high
confidence: medium
